From f78fd0940f255372956fb25237c1ee5cf55a8152 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 03:42:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kanban: trusted capsule admission for host_repo worktree
 cards on isolated backends

Native create and dispatch require host_repo for every worktree card and refuse
remote terminal backends, so a docker/runsc builder whose worktree is turned into
a task-local capsule could never be assigned one. This adds a host-owned,
in-process capsule registration (hermes_cli/kanban_capsule_admission.py) bound to
the board dispatch owner, exact profile homes, project id, repo root and a real
(non-stock) spawn transport. Native create consumes it via a create scope; the
dispatcher consumes it at claim and launch, and the launch only proceeds through
an authenticated, single-use owner rendezvous (gateway/session_kanban_rendezvous.py)
that hands the managed worker an observation fd bound to the exact run.

Unchanged: ordinary docker worktree create/dispatch stays refused, the stock
dispatcher refuses capsule cards, and nothing from card fields, model args or
config grants host_repo. Registration handles are immutable; the rendezvous is
probed (non-consuming) before scope resolution and consumed only after it.
---
